WEBVTT

00:02.960 --> 00:05.670
THE ELUSIVE
 SAMURAI

01:25.290 --> 01:29.960
THE ELUSIVE
 SAMURAI

01:54.730 --> 01:55.740
Lord Kunitoki.

01:57.320 --> 01:58.570
It's me, Muneshige.

01:59.110 --> 02:00.160
TOKIYUKI AND KUNITOKI'S UNCLE

02:00.240 --> 02:01.070
Uncle…

02:01.660 --> 02:03.540
What's the state of Kamakura?

02:03.620 --> 02:04.830
And what about Tokiyuki?

02:04.910 --> 02:08.040
I hear Lord Yorishige Suwa will help Tokiyuki escape.

02:08.120 --> 02:10.830
As for us, let's hurry and leave at the first light of day.

02:14.550 --> 02:16.550
-Uncle…
-Don't worry.

02:16.630 --> 02:19.590
The lower-ranked samurai shouldn't know our faces.

02:20.180 --> 02:21.590
I'll deceive them somehow.

02:21.680 --> 02:22.850
You stay hidden.

02:22.930 --> 02:24.260
That's too dangerous!

02:24.350 --> 02:28.690
Lord Takatoki entrusted me with you, his precious Hojo child.

02:29.190 --> 02:31.600
I will protect you even if I must lay down my life.

02:32.190 --> 02:33.480
Uncle…

02:33.570 --> 02:36.110
Yes, and above all,

02:36.610 --> 02:39.360
you are my precious little sister's child.

02:40.360 --> 02:43.370
If I fail, please run.

02:43.870 --> 02:45.290
Uncle!

02:51.170 --> 02:52.170
What?

02:58.920 --> 02:59.920
Uncle.

03:01.090 --> 03:02.090
Uncle!

03:02.800 --> 03:04.720
Uncle!

03:13.440 --> 03:14.480
Father!

03:14.560 --> 03:15.730
Everyone!

03:19.110 --> 03:21.740
Lord Tokiyuki. Lord Tokiyuki.

03:21.820 --> 03:23.280
Lord Tokiyuki!

03:24.070 --> 03:26.370
Lord Tokiyuki!

03:31.210 --> 03:32.790
Lord Tokiyuki.

03:33.790 --> 03:36.590
Lord Tokiyuki.

03:36.670 --> 03:39.130
Your face when you're asleep is so sweet.

03:39.210 --> 03:40.920
I could just eat you up.

03:41.010 --> 03:45.510
I know how much you like to watch children sleep, Father,

03:46.010 --> 03:48.850
-but Lord Tokiyuki is having a nightmare.
-There we go.

03:48.930 --> 03:50.100
Let's see!

03:50.180 --> 03:51.600
I think a peck on the cheek wouldn't hurt.

03:51.690 --> 03:52.520
GLARE

03:57.730 --> 03:59.570
What are you doing? What is wrong with you?

04:00.070 --> 04:03.910
Lord Tokiyuki, I expected as much from your escaping prowess.

04:03.990 --> 04:07.950
In the future, we call that a "Wake-up Prank."

04:08.030 --> 04:09.290
PRANK A SUCCESS!!!

04:09.370 --> 04:10.200
I don't care!

04:10.790 --> 04:12.790
This isn't the time to be playing around, Mr. Yorishige!

04:12.870 --> 04:15.790
You said we could hide in your territory,

04:15.880 --> 04:19.250
but we've just been taking cover in Kamakura for several days!

04:19.960 --> 04:25.550
That's because the exit of Kamakura is more tightly guarded than I thought.

04:26.760 --> 04:30.810
We have to be patient until their watch eases up.

04:32.730 --> 04:33.890
The watch, huh?

04:36.310 --> 04:39.440
<i>I recognize those standards…</i>

04:40.190 --> 04:43.990
<i>But the samurai under those banners, who had sworn allegiance to the Shogunate,</i>

04:44.070 --> 04:46.450
<i>betrayed us, just like that, and destroyed Kamakura.</i>

04:47.030 --> 04:50.120
<i>All under Lord Takauji's orders…</i>

04:50.740 --> 04:55.040
<i>To think beneath that kind smile of his, he was plotting such traitorous plans</i>

04:55.120 --> 04:56.620
<i>to destroy the Shogunate.</i>

04:59.170 --> 05:01.050
Don't worry, Lord Tokiyuki.

05:01.710 --> 05:03.380
In these clothes, we can trick them.

05:03.470 --> 05:06.800
We look like Shinto priests whose shrine was burned.

05:14.640 --> 05:15.850
Mr. Yorishige.

05:15.940 --> 05:19.900
You told me, "Take back your country by winning this game of tag

05:20.440 --> 05:23.360
with your excellent ability to run away."

05:23.940 --> 05:26.860
But samurai fight looking straight on.

05:26.950 --> 05:29.950
I've never heard of a samurai taking a country through a game of tag.

05:30.450 --> 05:33.080
You really think I can take back this country?

05:33.160 --> 05:35.410
That I can avenge everyone I loved?

05:35.500 --> 05:37.120
-Of course!
-You scared me!

05:37.620 --> 05:44.170
Through my divine eye, I see a future where you are a hero.

05:45.670 --> 05:50.640
So, Lord Tokiyuki, bear this burden for a little while longer.

05:51.760 --> 05:52.760
For now…

05:53.970 --> 05:55.020
FUTURISTIC GAME OF DICE

05:55.100 --> 05:57.480
let's play a game of dice while we wait!

05:57.560 --> 05:59.940
Shizuku, prepare the dice and game pieces!

06:00.020 --> 06:01.520
Yes, Father.

06:01.610 --> 06:03.270
I've never seen this game of dice.

06:03.360 --> 06:05.150
What's a God of Poverty?

06:05.240 --> 06:08.240
You'll get to learn when you play.

06:08.740 --> 06:11.160
Come on, Lord Tokiyuki. Join us.

06:15.160 --> 06:16.160
Huh?

06:18.000 --> 06:20.420
<i>I knew I couldn't trust those two.</i>

06:21.380 --> 06:24.670
<i>I have to find who remains of the Shogunate myself.</i>

06:38.890 --> 06:42.520
Man, there's nothing good here.

06:42.610 --> 06:44.820
One man's trash is another man's trash.

06:45.440 --> 06:48.610
You know, I saw that execution.

06:48.700 --> 06:54.280
Oh, yeah, was it Lord Kunitoki Hojo?

06:56.910 --> 06:59.160
Oh, yeah. The head came clean off.

06:59.790 --> 07:01.330
You have strange taste.

07:02.500 --> 07:03.750
You're lying!

07:04.500 --> 07:05.880
Huh?

07:06.800 --> 07:08.420
Who are you?

07:09.010 --> 07:10.130
There's no way!

07:10.220 --> 07:12.760
My brother… He can't be!

07:12.840 --> 07:14.220
Your brother?

07:14.300 --> 07:15.560
What do you mean your brother?

07:15.640 --> 07:17.390
You're talking about Lord Kunitoki?

07:18.020 --> 07:19.980
Whose kid are you?

07:20.060 --> 07:21.810
I
-

07:24.110 --> 07:27.280
This boy is an apprentice at my shrine.

07:27.780 --> 07:30.740
The Hojo family had favored us,

07:30.820 --> 07:33.700
so he can get worked up hearing Lord Kunitoki's name.

07:34.320 --> 07:35.330
Right?

07:36.700 --> 07:38.080
Yes.

07:40.500 --> 07:44.790
What exactly happened to Lord Kunitoki?

07:45.670 --> 07:50.670
You know, he was entrusted to his uncle, Muneshige Godaiin.

07:51.220 --> 07:57.060
He was hiding him, but then, he ratted Kunitoki's hiding spot out to Nitta's men.

07:57.640 --> 07:59.520
AWARD FOR BIGGEST TYRANT 1333
 GODAIIN

07:59.600 --> 08:01.060
<i>Having risen to power through his nephew,</i>

08:01.140 --> 08:03.230
<i>Muneshige Godaiin sold his own flesh and blood,</i>

08:03.310 --> 08:07.020
<i>the regent's nine-year-old son, to the enemy in the blink of an eye.</i>

08:07.110 --> 08:12.610
<i>The man went on to become one of the most brutal warlords in Japanese history.</i>

08:14.110 --> 08:16.490
Lord Kunitoki was a Hojo child.

08:17.240 --> 08:19.540
Beheading was his sentence.

08:20.200 --> 08:21.370
I saw it happen earlier.

08:22.330 --> 08:25.130
It was a pitiful death.

08:28.000 --> 08:29.300
Lord Tokiyuki?

08:35.720 --> 08:39.640
<i>Betrayal. Betrayal. Betrayal.</i>

08:41.140 --> 08:42.810
<i>I can't make sense of it.</i>

08:46.730 --> 08:49.900
<i>The Ashikaga family who served us for generations betrayed us.</i>

08:49.980 --> 08:52.990
<i>Our samurai retainers betrayed us.</i>

08:53.530 --> 08:55.030
<i>And now my own uncle betrayed us.</i>

08:55.990 --> 08:58.990
<i>There's not one person I can trust.</i>

09:02.080 --> 09:03.370
<i>Lord Tokiyuki.</i>

09:03.460 --> 09:05.080
-Lord Tokiyuki.
-Lord Tokiyuki.

09:05.170 --> 09:06.670
-<i>Lord Tokiyuki. </i>-Lord Tokiyuki.

09:06.750 --> 09:08.630
Lord Tokiyuki!

09:09.670 --> 09:12.630
Did my holy light bring you to your senses?

09:12.710 --> 09:15.260
Why do you keep shining at random times?

09:16.720 --> 09:17.760
I can see it.

09:18.390 --> 09:21.310
I can see a future where Muneshige Godaiin is sitting down.

09:22.560 --> 09:26.100
You know how I told you I can see the future with my holy power?

09:26.730 --> 09:28.360
Yeah, a rough vision on rare occasions.

09:28.440 --> 09:29.610
HERE WE GO
 GODAIIN - DUMB - ENEMIES

09:29.690 --> 09:33.190
<i>There's a lot of enemy soldiers around him, and he's well protected.</i>

09:33.940 --> 09:37.740
Where is Uncle now?

09:38.820 --> 09:40.410
Are you curious?

09:44.370 --> 09:45.620
Yes.

09:52.210 --> 09:53.670
In that case…

09:58.890 --> 10:00.180
let's go see.

10:05.890 --> 10:09.980
I'll show you what it means to win at a game of tag!

10:10.060 --> 10:11.940
Consider avenging your brother…

10:13.530 --> 10:16.860
your first step to reclaiming your country!

10:20.410 --> 10:21.410
Damn it!

10:21.490 --> 10:23.910
Why do you cast me aside?

10:24.410 --> 10:26.790
Don't you know I'm a man of great military success?

10:27.290 --> 10:29.040
He was a Hojo child!

10:29.620 --> 10:34.050
<i>Is it because he was the child of a concubine?</i>

10:34.130 --> 10:38.430
<i>The head of a concubine's child is of no worth to you?</i>

10:39.220 --> 10:43.890
<i>If killing Kunitoki isn't enough in my life's game of dice,</i>

10:43.970 --> 10:45.720
<i>I need to roll higher numbers.</i>

10:46.390 --> 10:50.560
<i>In that case, maybe I should aim for the rightful heir!</i>

10:51.350 --> 10:53.270
<i>I can do it.</i>

10:54.440 --> 10:58.650
<i>If I capture Tokiyuki, the true heir, and present him to them,</i>

10:59.780 --> 11:04.080
<i>everyone will have no choice but to recognize me!</i>

11:05.330 --> 11:08.870
His demonic behavior drove his friends away.

11:08.960 --> 11:10.670
Seems like he's lost everything.

11:11.370 --> 11:13.460
This greedy brute has turned into a demon

11:13.540 --> 11:15.590
who will chase you to the ends of the earth.

11:15.670 --> 11:17.840
Tokiyuki.

11:17.920 --> 11:20.970
Don't think you can outrun me.

11:21.050 --> 11:25.260
The first sure way to win at the game of tag is to know your enemy.

11:26.100 --> 11:28.100
Let's go back to the hideout, Lord Tokiyuki.

11:28.180 --> 11:29.100
Huh?

11:29.180 --> 11:31.770
I will bestow upon you the second sure way to win.

11:33.100 --> 11:35.270
They should be arriving soon.

11:35.360 --> 11:36.690
Right, Father.

11:38.320 --> 11:42.280
It's become easier to win now that we know what our enemy looks like, right?

11:44.240 --> 11:46.280
Do you not have confidence?

11:48.950 --> 11:53.080
I never took my martial arts training seriously.

11:53.170 --> 11:59.510
No worries. I have some friends I want to introduce to you.

12:00.130 --> 12:02.510
They will become your arms and legs.

12:02.590 --> 12:06.970
They will help you greatly on the battlefield.

12:09.100 --> 12:10.850
KAZUSA PROVINCE - SHIMOSA PROVINCE - MUSASHI PROVINCE

12:10.930 --> 12:14.480
All right, I'm gonna buy all of Shimosa's bean fields, getting double the revenue!

12:14.560 --> 12:17.190
Hey, don't pass the God of Poverty to me!

12:17.270 --> 12:19.860
He's about to become the Emperor God of Poverty too.

12:19.940 --> 12:22.200
I don't think they're going to be very helpful.

12:22.280 --> 12:24.780
And isn't that a game of dice from a distant future?

12:25.450 --> 12:27.120
PRODUCER

12:27.780 --> 12:29.330
Hi. It's nice to meet ya, young lord!

12:29.410 --> 12:31.790
My name is Kojiro Nezu. It's a pleasure!

12:32.290 --> 12:35.000
I'm Ayako Mochizuki. Nice to meet you, my lord.

12:35.710 --> 12:38.750
They are the children of the Nezu and Mochizuki families,

12:38.840 --> 12:40.260
two families who serve the Suwa family.

12:40.840 --> 12:42.590
And because they serve the Suwa family,

12:42.670 --> 12:46.010
they ultimately serve the Hojo family above them.

12:46.090 --> 12:50.890
And though both of them are your age, Lord Tokiyuki, they excel in martial arts.

12:50.970 --> 12:55.310
So please rely on them to avenge our enemy.

12:55.400 --> 12:59.150
I'm Tokiyuki Hojo. Nice to meet you.

12:59.230 --> 13:00.320
-Sir!
-Sir!

13:01.480 --> 13:03.650
<i>What did you think of Lord Tokiyuki?</i>

13:04.240 --> 13:05.820
He's so cute!

13:05.910 --> 13:07.570
I just wanna carry him around.

13:08.160 --> 13:10.200
He's definitely not strong.

13:10.290 --> 13:13.200
And it's a strange proposition coming from Lord Yorishige

13:13.290 --> 13:15.710
to serve someone whose family has just been annihilated.

13:15.790 --> 13:18.210
If he's not strong, we have to protect him.

13:23.970 --> 13:25.050
Right.

13:38.100 --> 13:43.570
Now, Lord Tokiyuki, shall we take on the demon that's after us?

14:05.840 --> 14:07.090
He's coming.

14:26.030 --> 14:29.950
<i>Oh, you look delectable.</i>

14:30.910 --> 14:33.240
Uncle Godaiin?

14:34.950 --> 14:37.000
Oh, Lord Tokiyuki!

14:37.080 --> 14:40.500
If it isn't my lord!

14:40.580 --> 14:43.380
Oh, I'm so glad you're safe.

14:43.460 --> 14:46.420
Lord Yorishige said he would bring you to safety around Suwa,

14:46.510 --> 14:47.630
so I thought you'd be here.

14:48.470 --> 14:49.550
Are you alone?

14:49.630 --> 14:53.640
Don't worry, your old Uncle Muneshige's here for you.

14:54.350 --> 14:55.890
Let's run away together.

14:56.730 --> 14:57.980
Uncle.

14:58.060 --> 14:59.270
Yes?

14:59.350 --> 15:02.190
Why did you betray my brother?

15:02.980 --> 15:03.860
Huh?

15:07.940 --> 15:10.200
I see, I see.

15:11.780 --> 15:13.160
-We almost had him!
-My lord!

15:14.370 --> 15:17.790
So you anticipated I would come looking for you,

15:17.870 --> 15:21.710
and hid some friends to ambush me to avenge your brother.

15:21.790 --> 15:25.380
You poised yourself as if you trusted me. It was quite impressive.

15:25.460 --> 15:27.840
To think a child could be so conniving!

15:28.470 --> 15:33.970
But you see, Lord Tokiyuki, the reason I was entrusted to guard Kunitoki

15:34.050 --> 15:37.470
was not only because I am his uncle and an important retainer!

15:38.060 --> 15:44.150
I was appointed his guard because I'm strong.

15:45.860 --> 15:50.610
Kill two brats, chop off your legs, and sell you out.

15:50.700 --> 15:53.490
That's how I'll win my game of dice!

15:53.570 --> 15:55.160
<i>The dice are cast.</i>

15:55.240 --> 15:57.160
<i>Is it a battle or just a game?</i>

15:57.240 --> 16:01.460
<i>It's a turbulent world of tag with our lives at stake.</i>

16:02.710 --> 16:05.090
<i>This is the first roll!</i>

16:05.170 --> 16:06.460
DEMON OF DICE MUNESHIGE GODAIIN

16:08.760 --> 16:11.340
What happened, Lord Tokiyuki?

16:11.420 --> 16:14.430
This is your chance to avenge your brother!

16:14.510 --> 16:17.390
Get off my lord, scumbag!

16:19.680 --> 16:21.350
You're in my way!

16:26.360 --> 16:27.480
-Hey!
-Damn it.

16:27.570 --> 16:29.820
Take this! Take that!

16:29.900 --> 16:31.650
My lord, get behind me!

16:31.740 --> 16:34.410
<i>I have no openings. And what mighty strength!</i>

16:34.490 --> 16:36.870
<i>I can't do anything while I protect myself and the Young Lord.</i>

16:37.700 --> 16:40.250
<i>What am I supposed to do after this, Mr. Yorishige?</i>

16:40.830 --> 16:42.660
<i>After all, we're just kids going up against a grown man.</i>

16:42.750 --> 16:45.630
<i>If our surprise attack fails, we stand no chance.</i>

16:48.550 --> 16:51.300
<i>It's just some kiddy sneak attack with just the three of them.</i>

16:51.880 --> 16:53.880
This is nothing!

16:53.970 --> 16:57.180
I'm quick to adapt to situations. That's one of my strengths.

16:57.260 --> 17:00.810
I'd betray even my lord's child if it meant saving my own life!

17:00.890 --> 17:03.270
Don't make it hard for me, Tokiyuki.

17:03.350 --> 17:07.020
Your brother didn't even put up a fight!

17:08.940 --> 17:13.570
<i>Ashikaga overthrew the Shogunate, and then came tumultuous times.</i>

17:18.870 --> 17:21.620
<i>When the board to the game of dice has been flipped,</i>

17:22.620 --> 17:26.290
<i>only those who can instantly adapt can survive!</i>

17:26.370 --> 17:27.380
Hmm?

17:34.550 --> 17:36.470
Tokiyuki!

17:37.050 --> 17:41.060
Tokiyuki, Tokiyuki, Tokiyuki, Tokiyuki!

17:41.890 --> 17:45.270
You're a relic of a bygone era.

17:45.850 --> 17:49.020
Accept your fate, and fuel my rise to the top!

17:54.070 --> 17:55.070
My lord!

17:55.650 --> 17:58.450
Kojiro, Ayako, retreat!

17:58.530 --> 17:59.780
-Huh?
-Why?

17:59.870 --> 18:01.660
Just listen to me and get back.

18:02.160 --> 18:05.410
You two should take a good look at this Young Lord.

18:05.500 --> 18:09.250
See who is more adaptable to tumultuous times.

18:17.130 --> 18:19.010
That's impressive, my lord.

18:19.090 --> 18:21.850
He's seeing through all those swift swings.

18:25.310 --> 18:28.310
And it looks like he's enjoying it.

18:34.820 --> 18:37.110
Those aren't moves you learn by training.

18:37.780 --> 18:39.160
His elusiveness…

18:41.950 --> 18:43.280
It's heaven-sent!

18:45.080 --> 18:47.290
Lord Tokiyuki isn't a coward.

18:48.290 --> 18:50.670
He genuinely enjoys the chase.

18:52.290 --> 18:54.500
<i>One misstep would be fatal.</i>

18:54.590 --> 18:55.920
<i>Capture would be instant death.</i>

18:56.010 --> 18:57.920
<i>His survival instinct is monstrous,</i>

18:58.010 --> 19:00.720
<i>which means his very soul can find joy in such crisis.</i>

19:01.510 --> 19:05.640
<i>Before the war, back when Kamakura was peaceful,</i>

19:05.720 --> 19:08.890
<i>the boy was amiable, modest, kind-hearted, and considerate.</i>

19:08.980 --> 19:10.400
<i>He hated conflict,</i>

19:10.480 --> 19:13.900
<i>and his habit of running away from his much-despised training was a shortcoming.</i>

19:13.980 --> 19:16.530
<i>He was an ordinary kid like any other.</i>

19:16.610 --> 19:21.240
<i>But on the battlefield, he becomes a gleeful monster,</i>

19:21.320 --> 19:23.950
<i>happily playing tag against the fiercest of the fierce.</i>

19:25.040 --> 19:31.290
Shizuku, Kojiro, Ayako, don't you think it'll be fun to serve a master like that?

19:31.370 --> 19:35.300
A general who's known for running away? I've never heard of that.

19:35.380 --> 19:39.170
But when you say it like that, Lord Yorishige, I guess it does sound fun.

19:39.260 --> 19:41.680
I just want to be his friend!

19:41.760 --> 19:42.890
Mm-hmm.

19:44.260 --> 19:45.390
All right, now.

19:45.470 --> 19:48.100
-Go give this another chance!
-Yes, sir!

19:48.680 --> 19:50.440
<i>You mustn't try to protect him.</i>

19:50.520 --> 19:52.810
<i>You have to trust his elusiveness.</i>

19:52.900 --> 19:54.310
<i>The trade-off…</i>

19:54.400 --> 19:55.400
SLUGGISH

19:55.480 --> 19:58.940
-<i>…is his attacks are very weak. </i>-You little brat!

20:00.070 --> 20:03.030
<i>Go create an opening for him to attack.</i>

20:07.240 --> 20:12.460
<i>If he's set on killing me by evading forever,</i>

20:13.040 --> 20:14.040
<i>then sooner or later…</i>

20:19.630 --> 20:21.550
-You guys!
-Time for offense!

20:25.220 --> 20:27.850
<i>My job isn't to protect the Young Lord from the enemy.</i>

20:28.350 --> 20:30.480
Tokiyuki!

20:32.310 --> 20:33.310
Whoa.

20:35.190 --> 20:36.770
You bastards!

20:40.320 --> 20:43.950
<i>Try to offer up the enemy while the Young Lord evades.</i>

20:44.030 --> 20:45.990
Now, my lord!

20:50.750 --> 20:54.620
<i>Brother, Father, citizens of Kamakura,</i>

20:55.210 --> 20:57.130
<i>this head isn't enough to avenge you.</i>

20:57.210 --> 20:58.710
<i>But at least…</i>

21:05.890 --> 21:07.350
<i>it'll make for a souvenir</i>

21:08.510 --> 21:10.350
<i>as you walk your path to the other side!</i>

21:19.020 --> 21:20.030
Huh?

21:21.030 --> 21:22.900
Where did it come from?

21:23.650 --> 21:25.950
I'm not going to be a hero.

21:26.030 --> 21:28.240
Even you're laughing at me.

21:28.320 --> 21:31.700
It's not that I'm making fun of you.

21:31.790 --> 21:35.620
Let's get inside already. I wonder what's for dinner.

21:37.790 --> 21:40.090
Oh, Tokiyuki!

21:41.880 --> 21:42.880
You can do it!

21:44.260 --> 21:47.140
If you try.

21:48.090 --> 21:49.430
What was that?

